// ⚠️ THIS REPO HAS TWO WRANGLER CONFIGS, AND WRANGLER PICKS THE WRONG ONE BY DEFAULT.
//
//   wrangler.toml   → the API WORKER (xlooop-api)  ← almost everything you want
//   wrangler.jsonc  → this file: a PAGES project for the functions/ feedback plane
//
// Wrangler auto-detects this file, sees `pages_build_output_dir`, and concludes the directory is a
// Pages project. Every Workers command then fails with a message that names the wrong cause:
//
//   [ERROR] It looks like you've run a Workers-specific command in a Pages project.
//
// That error is about THIS FILE, not about the command you ran. The fix is always the same:
//
//   npx wrangler tail xlooop-api --config wrangler.toml
//   npx wrangler secret list     --config wrangler.toml
//
// DO NOT DELETE THIS FILE to "clean up" the ambiguity. It is live config: functions/_middleware.js,
// functions/_lib and functions/api all exist, and the FEEDBACK_DB binding below is consumed by
// scripts/provision-feedback-d1-cloudflare.mjs and scripts/verify-customer-feedback-api-scenarios.mjs.
// Removing it breaks the feedback API deploy. An agent mid-debug on 260805 concluded it was stray and
// nearly recommended deletion; checking the consumers first is what stopped that.
//
// `pages_build_output_dir` points at dist-cloudflare/, which no script in this repo writes — see the
// note at scripts/verify-app-security-header-parity.mjs:64 documenting the same dead path. That is a
// separate, pre-existing question and is NOT a reason to delete this config.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "xlooop",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-05-17",
  "pages_build_output_dir": "dist-cloudflare",
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "FEEDBACK_DB",
      "database_name": "xlooop-feedback-test",
      "database_id": "9154ad92-084c-4573-8d08-78124f78e53f",
      "preview_database_id": "9154ad92-084c-4573-8d08-78124f78e53f"
    }
  ],
  "vars": {
    "FEEDBACK_REQUIRE_ACCESS": "1",
    "XLOOOP_FEEDBACK_ENVIRONMENT": "test"
  }
}
